    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full suite (`./mvnw test`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans, while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164. The change spans three files:\n\n1. **`E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 added a `display(String e164)` helper that splits the recognised country dial code (using the existing `CountryCode` enum) from the national number, then emits `+<countryCode> <national digits grouped in threes>` (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It returns `null` for null input and returns the value unchanged when the country code isn't recognised, so it degrades safely on non-E.164 data (e.g. unmigrated seed rows).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", ...)` plus a `toTelephoneDisplay(owner)` default method delegating to `E164Telephone.display(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nThe flow reuses the existing normalization: on create, `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` stores `telephone` as E.164 (`+61412345678`); the mapper now derives `telephoneDisplay` from that stored value on every read/response. The acceptance test asserting `telephone = \"+61412345678\"` and `telephoneDisplay = \"+61 412 345 678\"` passes, and `./mvnw test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
